# Route and Categorize Gmail Emails to Slack — required credential values
#
# This workflow does NOT read these as actual environment variables at runtime —
# n8n credentials are stored in n8n's own credential store, not in a .env file.
# This file just documents every value you need to have on hand when creating
# each credential in the n8n UI (Credentials -> New), and can double as a
# reference if you script credential creation via the n8n API/CLI instead.

# ── Gmail (trigger) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Credential name in n8n: "Gmail account"
# Credential type: gmailOAuth2
# Reuses the existing "Gmail account" credential in this n8n instance —
# nothing to create if you're running this alongside other Gmail-based agents.
# If you need a fresh one: Google Cloud Console -> OAuth client -> enable the
# Gmail API -> connect via n8n's "Sign in with Google" flow.

# ── OpenRouter (Llama 3 classification) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Credential name in n8n: "OpenRouter account"  <-- NOT yet created in this instance
# Credential type: httpBearerAuth (generic Bearer token auth)
# Get this from https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-ExampleOpenRouterApiKeyReplaceMe

# The Llama 3 model id to use for classification. See openrouter.ai/models for
# the full list of Llama 3 variants and current pricing.
OPENROUTER_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3-8b-instruct

# ── Slack (notifications) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Credential name in n8n: "Slack account"  <-- NOT yet created in this instance
# Credential type: slackApi (Bot User OAuth Token)
# Create a Slack app at https://api.slack.com/apps -> OAuth & Permissions ->
# add the "chat:write" bot scope -> install to your workspace -> copy the
# "Bot User OAuth Token" (starts with xoxb-).
# Then INVITE THE BOT into every channel below (Slack channels are private by
# default to bots that haven't been added), e.g. /invite @your-bot-name.
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-ExampleSlackBotTokenReplaceMe

# Target channels the workflow posts into (create these, or edit the
# "channelId" value in each Slack node in the workflow to your own channels).
SLACK_CHANNEL_URGENT=#urgent-emails
SLACK_CHANNEL_SALES=#sales-leads
SLACK_CHANNEL_SUPPORT=#support-tickets
SLACK_CHANNEL_OTHER=#general-inbox
